==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Green Egg: N104''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Surgeon Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
These forms are <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this unit is not meant to be used before its True Form. However, due to its somewhat low cost and quick recharge, it may be used as an emergency meatshield in [[Underground Labyrinth]] or [[Legend Quest]] if you have no use for its True Form.

==='''True Form'''===
Surgeon Cat serves as an anti-Floating crowd controller with decent health to boot. Unfortunately for Surgeon Cat, units such as [[Bishop Cat (Rare Cat)|Sanzo Cat]], [[Shaman Cat (Rare Cat)|Necro-Dancer Cat]], [[Delinquent Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Angry Delinquent Cat]] and even the generalist [[Onmyoji Cat (Rare Cat)|Thaumaturge Cat]] completely outclass them in that department with vastly superior effects and uptime. At best, Surgeon's Long Distance attacks may enable them to hit enemies the others fail to reach.

Surgeon Cat is also the intended counter to [[Pterowl Hazuku]], but it does a very poor job at this in comparison to [[Elder Beast Naala (Special Cat)|Awakened Naala]], [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Fishman Cat]] or [[Killer Cat (Rare Cat)|Radical Cat]], especially since Surgeon needs to be at least Lv.45 to survive an unweakened attack. They are also a non-gacha anti-Floating crowd controller, so they might be somewhat useful against Floating enemies for no gacha players. Overall, Surgeon Cat is a shabby unit who is not worth the high Behemoth Stone cost, with some rare use crowd-controlling Floating enemies in lieu of better options.

